Package: namzero-lite
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Raffaele P. Guidi <raffaele.p.guidi@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/raffaeleguidi/namzero-lite
Depends: libasound2 (>= 1.2.0) | libasound2t64, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-venv,
 libcap2-bin, alsa-utils, adduser, debconf
Recommends: bluez, network-manager, dnsmasq-base, sudo, python3-gi,
 gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-webkit2-4.1
Description: realtime guitar audio engine (NAM lite) for Raspberry Pi and Linux
 namzero-lite is a realtime guitar effect engine. It implements a fixed
 effect chain with NAM amp models, cabinet IRs, MIDI footswitch control and
 a local web UI. On a Raspberry Pi it runs as a systemd service (headless
 appliance); on a Linux desktop it runs from the application menu with a
 WebKit window and per-user configuration.
 .
 The same binary serves both installation modes; the mode is chosen with
 debconf and can be changed later with dpkg-reconfigure namzero-lite.
 .
 This package installs the engine, the Python web UI and BLE MIDI bridge,
 factory presets, the desktop launcher and systemd units. In service mode
 configuration lives in /etc/namzero (conffiles) and /var/lib/namzero.
